{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/972806-101-deviant-orgs","id":972806,"title":"101 Deviant Orgs","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Deviant: The Renegades"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-19T16:17:10-07:00","id":972806,"title":"101 Deviant Orgs","content":"So Deviant is coming sometime semi-soon, I think we should get some ideas for some Deviant Orgs out there. Silly, spooky, cool, what-have-you, sky's the limit.<br /> <br /> <b>1) The Archon Conglomerate:</b> Founded by Seer Magi, the company was taken over by their Proximus slave-apprentices, who have been attempting to manufacture Awakened Souls. They promised you unimaginable wealth, in exchange for a few drug treatments. Now you can see <i>everything</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>2) Last Dynasty International:</b> The old man paid you to steal some files about something called an &quot;amkhat&quot;. You were pretty upset to learn what exactly that <i>was</i>, and how sharp its teeth are. They were pretty upset, too, but as long as you steal for them, they say they'll make sure the poison doesn't spread any further.<br /> <br /> <b>3) The Church of the Dawn:</b> All your life, you worshiped it, along with your family in friends, in a compound in Nevada. Then it chose you as its priest. It showed you its glorious countenance, but all you saw was a demon born of fire and dread light, burning its profane scriptures into your skin in ancient holy tongues.<br /> <br /> <b>4) The Department of Postcognition:</b> According to the government, you died in the Gulf. According to the CIA, you're an analyst. According to you, well, you don't know what you are. All you know is that you can remember things that never happened to you. Every time you remember, the memories stay a little longer. They said you'd only work the job for five years and then get a cushy severance package. Then you remembered the last guy's last day.<br /> <br /> <b>5) The Intersect Program:</b> It started when your jackass former friend from Stanford sent you an email. Now you have the sum total of the CIA and NSA's intelligence hidden in the folds of your brain. Life at the Buy-More will never be the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":4488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","user":"malonkey1","date":". 09-19-2016, 08:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T17:24:06-07:00","id":972834,"title":"","content":"6) The Lazarenes: They said they prayed to the Lord for health and life eternal, but the only immortal here is the ancient thing that whispers in the dark. It was supposed to steal your body on that bloody altar, but somehow the ritual went haywire and you stole some of its power; now they're hunting you, because their master can't manifest until you're dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T17:00:58-07:00","id":974752,"title":"","content":"<b>7) Jefferson High Gaming Club:</b> You read the Chick Tracts and giggled with at them with your friends. Then you joined the gaming club. The character sheet looked weird, and you didn't understand any of the rules, but when you played, you went to another place. When you came back, some of that place almost seems to come back with you. You've touched power, but now the Lords of Baator want their due.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T17:09:09-07:00","id":974762,"title":"","content":"8) <b>Feral Labs: </b>You thought HG Wells made the doctor and his island up, you certainly didn't believe the online rumors that the CEO of your employer was a decedent of Dr Moreau. Well he was, and rather than making animals more like people, this doctor wanted to do the reverse, using serums he injected you and the other islands with over a period of months, changing your DNA with genes from various animals, each islander assigned a different species. You escaped the island along with a few other, but you have all become some sort of part animal freak, now the doctor and his company need to pay and the legacy of Moreau needs to end once and for all. After all, are you not men?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T17:08:46-07:00","id":975287,"title":"","content":"<b>9) Department T-91: </b>You came back from the war less than a man, literally. A burned piece of flesh with half his limbs missing after an ambush wiped out your unit. The bomb destroyed your body, the guilt your mind. One day the government came. They told you they could fix you, make you better, even reunite you with your men. You didn't want to believe them till you saw johnson coming through the door good as new. You accepted their offer and they took you to a secret facility where they put machines, wires and metal in your body. However, just when they were about to open your head, johnson stopped the operation and freed you. He told you the truth, they were creating human drones, not fixing soldiers. He stayed behind to give you a chance. You escaped, but you swore that you would be back. You failed your men once, you would not fail them again, and may god have mercy on however stands in your way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 11-20-2017, 02:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T18:23:38-07:00","id":975316,"title":"","content":"<b>10) The Emerald Circle: </b>You were working on something great. An alchemical cure for cancer, Parkinson's, dementia, any genetic disease in the world. The Circle found you, and promised you that they would help-and they did. At the cost of sapient beings condemned to endless misery because you needed their Vitriol. Even if you didn't die a little inside you cut open a Promethean, you knew attempting to help the world on the backs of a hundred or so homunculi was never going to work. So, you decided, you needed a way to sublimate your own life experiences into Vitriol-sacrificing the self for the good of the whole, instead of the completely blameless other. Good news-you now have an exciting enough life to the point where you don't lose much more of your actual self when you spit up the clear, miraculous acid. Bad news is, that's because you forgot something-the people who are willing to dissect sapient beings for resources are more than cold enough to ignore that fact that their subject and source used to be their buddy. At least it isn't Amalgam.<br /> <br /> <b>11) Cult of Elar'dhi: </b>What the hell were you <i>thinking? </i>Oh that's right-you're codependent, so when your lesbian crush (who was hetero, for extra pathetic points) killed herself, you fell apart so badly that when the Violinist told you of a song that could contact the dead, you were so desperate to hear her again you joined that <i>fucking </i>nutcase support group. Oh, they taught you the song all right-they also taught you the fact that it was also very much <i>alive, </i>a blind idiot dissonance that wanted (to the extent a disincarnate entity made of cosmic echos wants anything) to disrupt the song that holds the living and the dead apart. And you, oh so noble martyr, possessed the <i>exact </i>disorder needed to become the Herald of the Last Echo. The rite worked-you now have a voice in your mind made up of thousands of other voices, all telling you to destroy things and return all that makes sound into a harmony of discordance. And, uh, the fact that the Violinist and all of his gang are emo omnicidal psychos who deeply resent the fact that you still look and think human. That's not fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T06:24:43-07:00","id":975487,"title":"","content":"<b>12) Raziel Ltd-</b> you really needed the money. After all, why else would you sign up for that weird experiment offered by a weapon company? They say it was to check the &quot;user compatibility&quot; of their new technology- nothing serious, you won't even have to shoot anyone. Just some &quot;interface checks&quot; and such, and they were willing to pay well. Then, they gave you something in a shot- and the next thing you know you are strapped to a table, all of those weird tubes and probes and electrodes are connected to your body putting all kinds of fluids in and out while someone sits before you reading something from an old book in a language you don't recognize. It felt like your body was on fire- and maybe it was, because there was this golden light everywhere and some panic and pain as if someone was carving signs to your flesh. Things blew up, there was a hole in the wall and when you gained conscious, you were in an alley few blocks away from the company's office, you cloths are tattered and bloody (not your blood) and your skin was covered with scars of kabbalistic images which oozed some golden liquid (your blood), and on your forehead there was a serial number- 1-6-4. While you don't know what it means, and you don't know what happened- but apparently you are now &quot;company property&quot; and they want you back.<br /> <br /> This is the last time you sign up for something called as the &quot;NEPHILIM experiment&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 09-24-2016, 01:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T08:07:21-07:00","id":975518,"title":"","content":"13) Parascience Labs, a non profit set up a study to prove the existance of the human soul.<br /> <br /> You particapated in this study for cash, thinking was all bullshit, free money. But thevstrange occult experiments they used on changed the nature of your soul enough that they were able to remove it as a glowing liquid and then put it back inside you, after which the runes they'd tattooed on your arms and neck now glow with the same mutagenic light that your soul did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T15:02:06-07:00","id":976742,"title":"","content":"<b>14) Weapon Chi:</b> They said they wanted to help you understand your powers, control them, maybe give you a semblance of a normal life. Thankfully, their doctor had more scruples than the people in charge. Your control chip &quot;failed&quot;, you ran, and you've been running ever since.<br /> <br /> <b>15) The Order of the Quivering Palm:</b> You learned at the Monastery of the Sun Lotus, at your Master's feet for ten years, when your whole order was slain by the Quivering Palms, who sought an ancient forbidden technique that only the Master knew. You escaped with the last scroll of the technique. The Palms are deadly and driven, and your only hope may be the secrets of the scroll. But is the technique even worth protecting?<br /> <br /> <b>16) The Ordo Dracul:</b> You had a normal enough life, working as a geneticist, until you had a run-in with the last person you'd expect: Your great-great-great-great-grandpa. He promised you access to something that would assure a Nobel Prize, the blood of a vampire. You agreed, and he gave you his blood, both to study and to feed on. He thought he could keep you dependent, but you were smarter than that. You perfected a treatment that freed you from the need to feed, and even granted you a measure of &quot;granpappy's&quot; powers, provided you kept to a very particular cocktail of intravenous amino acids, synthetic proteins, and reverse transcriptase inhibitors. When you decided to keep this information to yourself, your granpappy was, to say the least, displeased, and his friends weren't too happy, either.<br /> <br /> <b>17) Tristan Cybernetics:</b> You were just walking by when somebody crashed a semi into the side of an office building. You were caught in the rubble, but somehow you managed to dig yourself free. It wasn't until you got an X-ray that you realized that...something...metal had bonded itself to your skeleton, something that didn't like the idea of being removed, even by its original owners.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T20:52:33-07:00","id":1152690,"title":"","content":"<b>18) The Phyrexian Incursion:</b> You didn't know what happened at first. One moment, you were playing a card game, the next, you had killed you best friend and run off into the night. You woke up to find that parts of your body have been replaced with hideous contraptions dripping with a strange oil. The part the really scares you is how okay you seem with this.<br /> <br /> <b>19) The Hungry Ones:</b> You were born as livestock. Your whole life, you were raised for a very particular spiritual disorder, in order to feed a race of gods known only as the Hungry. When time came for the feeding, you somehow fed upon them, worsening your own spiritual state and warping your body to resemble their terrible forms. Now the ones who raised you are after you, and you're not sure if they want to kill you or worship you. And after seeing their rituals, you're not sure which one's worse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T21:12:13-07:00","id":1152701,"title":"","content":"<b>20: The Cheiron Group:</b> Internship your ass! Whatever they put into you, they didn't stop putting it in. Surgery after surgery, graft after graft, you can barely remember what your old body looks like some days. They threw around phrases like &quot;interstatial acquisition&quot;, &quot;hemophiliac augment&quot;, words that sounded medical but turned out to be anything but. Afraid and unsure of what to do, you managed to escape one night from the labs you and others like you were being held in. You know that if they find you, you're as good as dissected. Is there anyone that can help at this point?<br /> <br /> <b>21: VASCU:</b> Your mind, you know they did something to your mind. Your brain was normal, you know that. You remember that they talked to you, said you could become someone good. They put you in a chair, gave you injections, but your mind is hazy in-between then and now. Something changed, your whole body changed. You don't feel like you know you used to feel, right? Why does your body feel one way and your brain another? You look like other people, but inside your head there's a screaming thing trying to claw it's way out. And you can see it changing your body more and more each day.<br /> <br /> <b>22: Les Mysteries:</b> You trusted the spirits, thought they were something good for you and your loved ones. They convinced you to find others like you, other people who had the same gifts. Then it happened, one night the spirits wanted more than you were willing to give. They took your body, turned it into a shrine to self. By the time your allies found you the spirit's work was irreversible. Somehow you survived, when everyone around you said that you should by all rights be dead. Is there any going back?<br /> <br /> <b>23: The Lucifuge:</b> Not all human, not all demon. You were born with cursed blood, but soon it became a cursed body. Your &quot;family&quot; tried to help you learn control, to become something more than just another tool of Satan's works. It didn't take. One night you realized that you weren't able to shift your body back to being fully human, that whatever your demon-parent was, they had left an indelible mark not only on your soul but your flesh. It's going to rip you apart one day, and no one can tell you any way to stop it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T22:32:50-07:00","id":1152717,"title":"","content":"<b>24: Human Enhancement Laboratory (H.E.L) (TFV) </b><br /> (Insert Classified Disclosure here)<br /> <br /> Test subjects are to come from (in order of preference): Injured TFV personnel, TFV volunteers, injured US Armed Forces personnel, hand-selected volunteers.<br /> The goal of this laboratory are 1. To restore injured personnel to fighting fitness. 2. To improve on normal human combat capabilities 3. To improve the human condition.<br /> <br /> The Human Enhancement Laboratory is authorized to experiment with any and all means of improving the abilities of these soldiers. Currently promising fields include cybernetics, psyconic injections, and T.H.O.R injections. Other fields may receive funding upon review. As per TFV order ###, all subjects are to be fitted with chips capable of suppressing either the individual or their abilities upon activation. Research is ongoing in improving the capabilities of these chips, currently 25.37% have malfunctioned upon activation, with a further 5% malfunctioning in the field.<br /> <br /> There is no truth to the rumors that unwilling participants are currently used in any experiments, nor have they ever been used for preliminary testing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T23:08:00-07:00","id":1152720,"title":"","content":"Three I came up with for an old thread in the Hunter forum:<br /> <br /> 25. You don't know what to do. You believed in the Vanguard Unit's mission - you still do, how could you not? But that serum they stuck you with did things you - twisted your mind and body until you don't know the difference between your own flesh and madness. It can't be allowed to go on, but should you destroy VASCU or just the Wintergreen process?<br /> <br /> 26. You don't really have much of a grudge against the Talbot Group: they managed to get that monster out of you, but you're not really any better off with the tear in your soul it left behind. The Group want to help you, but you've had enough of their help. But at least they don't want to <i>hurt</i> you. Not like some of the others who've started following you.<br /> <br /> 27. They said you owed a debt to society, and that society owed a debt to the land. The deal was supposed to be that you anchored something, but you didn't really get the details. Whatever it was, it was too big - it broke you open. But you survived. And now society owes you - starting with those Lord Steward bastards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T23:11:33-07:00","id":1152722,"title":"","content":"28) Hotel Mascaron. They always made more sense as an antagonist group than a Hunter group, although the Sleepers in <i>Hurt Locker</i> do step on these toes a little.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T23:50:23-07:00","id":1152727,"title":"","content":"Because of a certain superhero show I'm watching...<br /> <br /> 29) Bugster Genome Project<br /> <br /> It started with the headaches. And then the fevers. And then the passing out. And then the hallucinations: what you could best describe as little yellow men jumping out of your skin. When you were taken the hospital, the doctors had no idea what you had. They know you had a viral infection, yes, but none they had seen before. Then the men in suits and lab coats came. They tell you that you're Patient Zero of a brand new virus. And that if something isn't done NOW, there will be an epidemic the likes of not seen in centuries. Luckily for you, they have some new experimental medical technology that they believe will be just the thing that'll pick you back up. Make you as good as new...<br /> <br /> ...except not really. While some of your symptoms have resided some are still there. Namely the headaches and the hallucinations. And your body has been feeling stranger too in general: lighter, but weight-ier, if that made any sense. Not helping were the regular rotation of new and different people each day during your stay, and how you were constantly referred to as &quot;the Subject&quot;. Having enough of it, and deciding that you felt well enough anyways, you ended up leaving...and knew something was off when you were met by men with guns as you left.<br /> <br /> You managed to escape with your life, now on the run from the Genome Project that would like nothing more then their subject and their experimental medical equipment back. Of course you have bigger things to worry about<b></b>: those headaches still bug you from time to time. And your hallucinations seem to be acting up again: since you seem to see the tiny yellow men crawling on the skin on OTHER people since you left.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T00:15:17-07:00","id":1152729,"title":"","content":"The Embassy of Exiles: Gentlemen's Club for Disgraced Gentry.<br /> Charlatans are predominantly lonesome hunters too narcissistic and whimsical to cooperate with one another without it ending in betrayals and bloodshed, so it isn't surprise it took so long for them to form an Embassy. Why did they do it?<br /> So that they could trade Tokens and broken pieces of Regalia, crack hidden escape clauses of their exile contracts, and engage in miniature traditions of Wild Hunt and Games of Immortals. And in the end of the day, while stuck in Ironside even the proudest of Kindly Folk will come begging for a reminder of their homeworld.<br /> <br /> You have been unfortunate enough to get caught by them, dragged screaming into their dimly lit surgical theater, bound with thorny vines, drugged and transformed. You haven't become a Changeling, no, the Charlatans are too weak in comparison to their dignified Kin, but they have learned during their time on Earth and patch what their magic doesn't cower with inventions of modern medicine, science(!), and some self-taught improvised engineering.<br /> Now you live, with worst of two worlds with hardly any of the good (and even less of the weird). So, are you hunter or one of the hunted?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12082,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","user":"Weird","date":". 10-25-2017, 03:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T13:41:47-07:00","id":1152916,"title":"","content":"Sinclair Pharmaceuticals<br /> <br /> There's no sinister plots here. Just a brilliant scientist who's dedicated to the betterment of mankind through medical research and the reasonably honest and ethical corporate empire he's built. Oh, he's also a member of Null Mysteriis who considered Cheiron but decided they were too evil for his tastes. But mindless supernatural plants, or paying supernaturals for blood samples, that's perfectly ethical. It's a bit risky but with proper safeguards and procedures there's no reason it can't work.<br /> <br /> And it did work. Until an old college buddy called up begging for help with his daughter's late stage cancer. &quot;What's the worst that can happen?&quot; He said. &quot;She's already dying.&quot; He said. So some experiments were tried, and the daughter ended up with a damaged soul and awesome powers. She loves having her health back, loves having powers. But Sinclair is wrecked by guilt, he knows about Deviants, he knows what can happen to them if they loose control. He thinks it's a fate worse than death, which is why he's willing to ignore little things like consent if it means curing his patient.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 02-05-2020, 12:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T14:14:24-07:00","id":1152939,"title":"","content":"<b>10) Tenno: </b>They still talk about the slaughter, after all this time, about how you and several others killed your <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">masters</span>. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">They</span> didn't make you, not exactly. You were afflicted with a condition, a horrible illness and madness that threatened to claim you body and soul. <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">They</span> hated you, decreed you to be demons, but in a moment of desperation when their creations rebeled against <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">them</span>, <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">they</span> turned to you and made you into weapons, another cog in their machine of war.<span style=\"color:#DAA520\"> They</span> tolerated your existence only out of necessity, but you knew that the war wouldn't last forever.<br /> So you killed <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">them</span> first, shattered their control, shattered their rule, the moon ran red with their blood.<br /> <br /> And then you slept, locked yourself away from a world that no longer needed you up until now. You awoke and found yourself in a changed world; now you are hunted by those that want to succeed your masters.<br /> <br /> <br /> (Incredibly vague rendition of the plot of Warframe to be more archetypical and valid in other settings. Essentially, the adventures of what happens when Deviants succeed in defeating their creators.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 10-25-2017, 05:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T21:34:17-07:00","id":1153050,"title":"","content":"this looks fun - contributing a few of my own... <hr /><br /> <b>Balam Medical Research Corporation</b><br /> You were serving a 3 -5 year stretch in a Mexican prison, but as a <i>gringo</i> from north of the border with no money and no friends, you didn't expect to make it that long. When the doctors appeared and offered you a way out of prison and back home, you leapt at it. Now your days consist of unbearable pain as bone and flesh warp into something bestial and inhuman. Maybe if you can get out of this place, maybe if you can get home, maybe someone can fix you.<br /> <br /> <b>Ideal Inc.</b><br /> It's a hell of a thing to realize your entire existence is a lie. Your education, your childhood friends, the accident that killed your parents, the dream boyfriend..all fabrications. Your not even a real person, but something born in test tube and custom grown to satisfied the needs of some rich lonely bastard. But you are alive, you are aware, and you will be <i>damned</i> before you become the toy they made you to be.<br /> <br /> <b>The Maenad Virus</b><br /> You feel fine. You feel better than fine. You have never felt more energized and aware of your own body. You feel stronger and faster than should be possible and pain seems like a distant memory. Sure your constantly hungry, and you are certain you were being followed yesterday. But isn't a little paranoia and a worked up appetite a small price to pay to feel like a God?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T21:40:54-07:00","id":1153053,"title":"","content":"There's always FEAR Corp and all the lovely rival corporations as well....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T04:52:45-07:00","id":1153117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/972806-101-deviant-orgs?p=1153050#post1153050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Ideal Inc.</b><br /> It's a hell of a thing to realize your entire existence is a lie. Your education, your childhood friends, the accident that killed your parents, the dream boyfriend..all fabrications. Your not even a real person, but something born in test tube and custom grown to satisfied the needs of some rich lonely bastard. But you are alive, you are aware, and you will be <i>damned</i> before you become the toy they made you to be.<br /> <br /> <b>The Maenad Virus</b><br /> You feel fine. You feel better than fine. You have never felt more energized and aware of your own body. You feel stronger and faster than should be possible and pain seems like a distant memory. Sure your constantly hungry, and you are certain you were being followed yesterday. But isn't a little paranoia and a worked up appetite a small price to pay to feel like a God?</div> </div> </div> </div>So now those Horrors are actually Deviants? Interesting! Will you stat them out as Deviants when the game comes out?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T17:23:56-07:00","id":1153335,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: Deviants and Horrors</b><br /> <br /> One of the things I am looking forward to with Deviant is a system that has a high degree of flexibility - its part of why I enjoy the Horror rules so much. With that in mind, its not difficult to cast thematically appropriate Horrors as Deviants instead. While I probably won't start re-fitting all my Horrors as Deviants, it does open some very intriguing Storytelling opportunities that have me eagerly awaiting the Deviants release (or even the next teaser).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T01:11:44-07:00","id":1153885,"title":"","content":"Oh, speaking of Deviants and Horrors, what about the Horrors of Beast than those of the generic WoD. A human cult of the Dark Mother, trying to create Beasts as a sacrament, via a ritual meant to draw a Horror into a person. But they don't realise that Beasts are already Beasts-in-waiting before the Horror shows up, and only a few very rare cases do they perform their rites on a suitable subject. Usually, nothing happens. But a few times, the collision between Horror and soul results in a cracked soul and leaking power faintly resembling the monster that was almost forced into them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}